"肯定\" (definitely) addition — minor. \"which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago\" → \"那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方\" — fine. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率\" — fine. \"它\" refers to key, fine. The \"肯定\" addition — is it substantive? It changes modality slightly. Could be UNCERTAIN ADDITION. I'll maybe skip; it's minor. Actually \"I'll have everything prepared\" is a commitment; \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as \"I will definitely have everything prepared\" — fine actually, \"肯定\" = definitely will. Acceptable. Skip.\n\nQ028: \"unhallowed morass\" → \"不洁沼泽\" fine. \"inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" fine. \"find the source\" → \"找到这一切的源头\" adds \"这一切的\" — compatible. \"你效力的时候到了\" — \"you are called to serve\" — okay. Empty.\n\nQ029: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。\" — Source: only hatchlings so far (i.e., they've only found hatchlings). Target: \"never encountered hatchlings\" — INVERTED! 从未遇上 = never encountered, but source says nothing but hatchlings = only hatchlings. That's a big DIRECTION/VALUE defect. FINDING.\n\nAlso \"dragonhide to cover a dragon\" → \"龙皮连一条龙都盖不住\" fine. \"spared no expense\" fine. \"dwarven Thronesmen\" → \"钢铁王座\" fine-ish. \"wyrmic\" → \"龙战士\" fine. \"turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons\" → \"把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙\" — okay. Main finding: 从未遇上 vs nothing but hatchlings.\n\nQ030: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — adds \"我的\" (my). Source is generic \"report for bad behavior\". Hmm, likely a UI label for reporting a player's bad behavior. Adding \"我的\" changes meaning to reporting oneself. That's a SUBJECT/REFERENT defect. FINDING? Evidence supports: source has no \"my\". But could be contextually about reporting someone else... \"举报我的不良行为\" = report my bad behavior — that seems wrong; you'd report someone else's behavior. But without context, adding \"我的\" is unsupported and flips meaning. Rule 3: additions compatible with visible evidence that can't be judged wrong... \"我的\" can't be directly contradicted but it's a specific referent not in source. Actually rule 3 says new info compatible and unable to be judged wrong by visible evidence is NOT a defect. Adding \"my\" is judgeable? The source is impersonal; \"my\" makes it self-report. I'd say FINDING with SUBJECT: remove \"我的\". Hmm risky. I think it's a real defect: UI \"Report for bad behavior\" is a button to report bad behavior; \"举报我的不良行为\" is nonsense direction. I'll report as FINDING SUBJECT... Actually it could be ADDITION. I'll use ADDITION with correction \"举报不良行为\".\n\nQ031: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — \"Place\" vs \"丢弃\" (discard/drop). ACTION defect. FINDING: 丢弃 = discard, place = 放置. Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\"\n\nQ032: \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" → \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\" — adds \"在龙之贪婪成就中\" — huge ADDITION of achievement name not in source. FINDING ADDITION.\n\nQ033: fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — inverted! not let you down vs definitely disappoint. FINDING DIRECTION. Correction: \"我不会让你失望的！\"\n\nQ035: \"Got to wave 50\" → \"生存至第20轮\" — 50 vs 20, VALUE. FINDING.\n\nQ036: \"Now, this is impressive!\" → \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — adds \"这个发现\" (this discovery). Source just \"this is impressive\". Minor addition; \"this\" could refer to discovery. Compatible addition → not defect. Empty. Hmm, \"Now, this is impressive\" — could refer to anything. \"这个发现\" specific. Rule 3 allows. Empty.\n\nQ037: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" → \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心\" (ambition) loses \"power\"; \"wild\" dropped. \"权力与永恒生命的狂野梦想\". Ambition ~ dream of power? Reasonably close; \"power\" omitted but 野心 covers ambition for power? Hmm. Also \"狂野\" omitted. I'd say minor, maybe skip. Could report OMISSION of \"power\". I'll skip — 野心 reasonably implies. Empty.\n\nQ038: \"Kickin' it old-school\" → \"现代风格\" (modern style) — inverted! old-school vs modern. FINDING DIRECTION. Correction: \"复古怀旧风\" or \"老派风格\".\n\nQ039: fine. \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" fine.\n\nQ040: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" → \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"in orbit\" (轨道上) vs \"在地面上\" (on the ground) — inverted location. FINDING DIRECTION. Correction: \"使其稳定在轨道上\".\n\nAlso \"Abashed Expanse\" → \"次元浮岛\" — proper noun translated differently; without external knowledge, source is a proper name; target names it \"dimensional floating island\" — that's a rendering, can't judge without context? \"Expanse\" = 广阔区域, not 浮岛. Hmm, in ToME the Abashed Expanse is a zone. Translation \"次元浮岛\" — questionable but rule 1 says only objective issues from visible text. \"Expanse\" ≠ 浮岛 (floating island). But proper nouns are often localized creatively. Could be UNCERTAIN. The orbit/ground is clear FINDING. Maybe also UNCERTAIN for the name. I'll include one candidate for orbit/ground, maybe second UNCERTAIN for name. Actually adding it might be over-reporting. The main defect is orbit→ground. I'll include just that.\n\nQ021 correction: \"你看不懂的一种语言\" — target structure: \"which you do not understand\" modifies language. Correction: \"即使你不懂这种语言，也无法理解：...\" Hmm actually source fragment \"which you do not understand: 'Sho ch'zun...'\" — the text is in a language you don't understand. Target says even if you understand it you can't understand. Correction: \"这种语言你无法理解\" or \"你看不懂这种语言：\". I'll write: \"你无法理解这种语言：\"\n\nQ023: \"peer out\" — eyes look out through slot. \"凝视着他\" asserts gaze at \"him\". Correction: \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\". Verdict FINDING, claim ACTION or REFERENT. I'll use REFERENT? The added \"他\" plus direction. Use ACTION: peer out = 向外窥视, not staring at him. Actually two aspects: added object \"他\" and direction outward. I'll use DIRECTION or REFERENT. Pick REFERENT with correction removing 他.\n\nHmm, is it strong enough? \"peer out\" clearly means look outward from the opening. \"凝视着他\" — staring at him. Yes, direction/object contradiction. FINDING.\n\nQ025: leave empty. Actually reconsider \"orbs of command\" — in game it's 指挥宝珠. But \"水晶球\" — orb translated as 水晶球. Rule 3 protects. Empty.\n\nQ030 verdict: I'll go FINDING ADDITION? Or UNCERTAIN? The phrase \"Report for bad behavior\" — target \"举报我的不良行为\". Without context, whose behavior? Ambiguous. \"my\" is a specific addition that flips potential meaning. I think FINDING is justified: adding \"我的\" makes it self-reporting which is odd; but is it objectively wrong? Could be a button in a menu where you report the NPC's bad behavior... \"my\" would be wrong then. Given source is neutral, adding first-person possessive is an ADDITION defect. I'll report FINDING.\n\nHmm, rule 3: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\" Can \"我的\" be judged wrong by visible evidence? The source doesn't indicate whose behavior; \"my\" is compatible in the sense that the source doesn't exclude it... This rule would protect it. But the source is a generic label \"Report for bad behavior\" — the addition of a first-person referent changes the action's meaning in a way that... Honestly by the strict rules, \"my\" can't be directly contradicted. I'll mark UNCERTAIN. Hmm. Actually let me think about the source: likely a UI option when interacting with... In ToME there's \"Report for bad behavior\" maybe in p уточcases? I shouldn't rely on external. I'll go UNCERTAIN ADDITION.\n\nQ036: skip.\n\nQ037: skip. Actually reconsider \"wild dreams of power\" → \"野心\" — power omitted. \"power and eternal life\" both listed; target \"野心并获得永恒的生命\" — ambition + eternal life. Power → ambition is a narrowing but arguably compatible (ambition for power). Wild dropped. I'll skip.\n\nQ032: \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中\" — clear ADDITION FINDING. Also \"Amassed\" vs 积累 fine. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\"\n\nNow output 20 items in order Q021–Q040.\n\nFindings list:\n- Q021: FINDING (DIRECTION) — \"即使你懂得这种语言\" vs \"which you do not understand\".\n- Q022: empty.\n- Q023: FINDING (REFERENT) — 凝视着他 vs peer out.\n- Q024: empty.\n- Q025: empty.\n- Q026: empty.\n- Q027: empty (or note 肯定). Empty.\n- Q028: empty.\n- Q029: FINDING (VALUE/DIRECTION) — 从未遇上幼龙 vs Nothing but hatchlings. Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到幼龙。\"\n- Q030: UNCERTAIN (ADDITION) — 我的.\n- Q031: FINDING (ACTION) — 丢弃 vs Place.\n- Q032: FINDING (ADDITION) — 在“龙之贪婪”成就中.\n- Q033: empty.\n- Q034: FINDING (DIRECTION).\n- Q035: FINDING (VALUE).\n- Q036: empty.\n- Q037: empty.\n- Q038: FINDING (DIRECTION) — 现代风格 vs old-school.\n- Q039: empty.\n- Q040: FINDING (DIRECTION) — 地面上 vs in orbit.\n\nEvidence must be verbatim from source. Write JSON.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q021\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"DIRECTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\",\n          \"correction\": \"你无法理解这种语言\",\n          \"evidence\": \"which you do not understand\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文说的是一种你看不懂的语言（do not understand），译文反转为“即使你懂得……也无法理解”，语义方向相反。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q022\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文与原文内容、语气及语序一致，未见客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q023\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"REFERENT\",\n          \"target_span\": \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\",\n          \"correction\": \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\",\n          \"evidence\": \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文 peer out 表示眼睛从门缝向外张望，无“他”这一对象；译文添加“凝视着他”，方向与指涉对象均与原文不符。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q024\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文准确对应原文，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q025\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文完整传达原文请求与内容，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q026\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文与原文含义一致，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q027\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文信息完整，关键条件与结果均与原文相符，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q028\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文忠实传达原文指令与背景，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q029\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"DIRECTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\",\n          \"correction\": \"到目前为止只遇到了幼龙\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文 Nothing but hatchlings 表示到目前为止遇到的只有幼龙，译文“从未遇上幼龙”含义完全相反。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q030\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"ADDITION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"举报我的不良行为\",\n          \"correction\": \"举报不良行为\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Report for bad behavior\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文为泛指的“举报不良行为”，译文添加第一人称“我的”，指涉对象为原文所无，是否成立取决于未见的使用语境。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q031\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"ACTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"将物品丢弃到哪里\",\n          \"correction\": \"将物品放置到哪里\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Place the object where?\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文 Place 表示放置，译文“丢弃”为不同的动作，改变了询问的操作内容。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q032\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"ADDITION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\",\n          \"correction\": \"积累了3000金币\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文只说明积累3000金币，译文添加“在‘龙之贪婪’成就中”这一原文没有的成就限定信息。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q033\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文与原文含义、数值一致，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q034\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"DIRECTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"我一定会让你失望的\",\n          \"correction\": \"我绝不会让你失望的\",\n          \"evidence\": \"I will not let you down!\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文为否定式承诺“不会让你失望”，译文反转为“一定会让你失望”，语义完全相反。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q035\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"VALUE\",\n          \"target_span\": \"生存至第20轮\",\n          \"correction\": \"到达第50波\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文数值为 50，译文写作“第20轮”，数值不符。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q036\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文传达赞叹语气，添加的“发现”与原文指示含义相容，无可判定的客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q037\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文整体传达原文含义，成就与成为巫妖的结果均一致，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q038\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"DIRECTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"现代风格\",\n          \"correction\": \"复古怀旧风格\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Kickin' it old-school\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文 old-school 指老派、怀旧风格，译文“现代风格”含义相反。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q039\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文与原文条件（已死亡状态下击杀BOSS）一致，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q040\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"DIRECTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"使其稳定在地面上\",\n          \"correction\": \"使其维持在轨道上\",\n          \"evidence\": \"to maintain it in orbit\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文为维持“在轨道上”（in orbit），译文写作“稳定在地面上”，位置关系与原文相反。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai-standard-cn","model":"glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":2420,"output":4513,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2983,"totalTokens":6933,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787984146332,"responseId":"202608291415465e1ce9f65a2d4fdb","rawStopReason":"stop"},"toolResults":[]}
{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"你是双语翻译审核员。逐条比较英文 source 与中文 target，判断是否存在客观、实质性的翻译缺陷。\n\n规则：\n\n1. 只报告可由本请求中可见文本直接支持的客观问题；不要依赖外部知识、仓库记忆、猜测或风格偏好。\n2. 若条目包含 source_context，可把它作为与 source 同等有效的源码证据；若没有，则只能使用 source 与 target。\n3. 新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\n4. FINDING 表示证据足以确定存在缺陷；UNCERTAIN 仅用于证据指向问题但仍有真实歧义；没有可报告的客观问题时 candidates 为空数组。\n5. 一个条目可报告多个相互独立的候选。不要因为发现一个问题而停止检查，也不要让错误候选抵消正确候选。\n6. 每个候选的 target_span 必须逐字出现在 target 中；evidence 必须逐字出现在 source，或在该条目存在时逐字出现在 source_context 中。\n7. 保持输入顺序和 neutral_id 完全不变。严格输出符合给定 schema 的 JSON，不要输出 Markdown 或额外说明。\n\n缺陷类型：VALUE、DIRECTION、CONDITION、SUBJECT、REFERENT、TIMING、SCOPE、ACTION、STATE、ORDER、OMISSION、ADDITION、OTHER。\n\n输出 JSON Schema（逐字遵守）：\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"items\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 20,\n      \"maxItems\": 20,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"required\": [\"neutral_id\", \"candidates\", \"observation\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"neutral_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^Q[0-9]{3}$\"},\n          \"candidates\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"maxItems\": 4,\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\n              \"required\": [\"verdict\", \"claim_type\", \"target_span\", \"correction\", \"evidence\"],\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"FINDING\", \"UNCERTAIN\"]},\n                \"claim_type\": {\"enum\": [\"VALUE\", \"DIRECTION\", \"CONDITION\", \"SUBJECT\", \"REFERENT\", \"TIMING\", \"SCOPE\", \"ACTION\", \"STATE\", \"ORDER\", \"OMISSION\", \"ADDITION\", \"OTHER\"]},\n                \"target_span\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                \"correction\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"observation\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n输入 JSON：\n{\"schema_version\":\"source-context-controlled-confirmation-request-a-v2\",\"items\":[{\"neutral_id\":\"Q021\",\"source\":\"which you do not understand: #{italic}#'Sho ch'zun Eyal mor donuth, ik ranaheli donoth trun ze.'#{normal}#\",\"target\":\"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解：#{italic}#'Sho ch'zun Eyal mor donuth, ik ranaheli donoth trun ze.'#{normal}#\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q022\",\"source\":\"The Creator. The God who made this world, He who watched silently as the races fought and burnt the land.\\nHe who felt great sorrow for this world. He who shall now shatter the barriers of this world to remake it, only better!\\nThe staff will allow us to drain enough energy from this world to open the portal to the Void and summon Him through!\\nYou cannot stop us now!\",\"target\":\"造物主，创造这个世界的神。他默默注视着各个种族争战不休，将大地付之一炬。\\n他为这个世界深感悲痛。如今他将击碎这个世界的屏障，将它重塑得更加美好！\\n这根法杖将让我们得以从这个世界抽取足够的能量，打开通往虚空的传送门并召唤他降临！\\n你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q023\",\"source\":\"#LIGHT_GREEN#*A slot in the door opens and a pair of wild eyes peer out.*#WHITE#\\nWhat do you want, @playerdescriptor.race@?\",\"target\":\"#LIGHT_GREEN#*门上开了一个小洞，一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他。*#WHITE#\\n你想干什么，@playerdescriptor.race@？\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q024\",\"source\":\"Aeryn, are you well?\",\"target\":\"艾琳，你还好么？\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q025\",\"source\":\"Thanks, my lady. I have not been able to find all of the orbs of command in my travels; could you have some of your men search for me?\",\"target\":\"谢谢，我的女士。我没能找到所有的指令水晶球；请问你可以让你们的人来帮我寻找一下吗？\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q026\",\"source\":\"Number of items to make\",\"target\":\"制作的物品数量\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q027\",\"source\":\"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared. Oh, take this. #LIGHT_GREEN#*He hands you a key*#WHITE# It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago. If you happen to find a text in the ruins entitled \\\"Inverted and Reverted Probabilistic Fields,\\\" return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically.\",\"target\":\"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。哦，带上这个。#LIGHT_GREEN#*他交给你一把钥匙。*#WHITE#它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方。要是你在废墟之中找到一份标题是《反转与复原概率场》的文献，请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q028\",\"source\":\"@playername@, you are called to serve. The nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless.\\nYou must go there and find the source.\",\"target\":\"@playername@，你效力的时候到了。附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动。\\n你必须去那里，找到这一切的源头。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q029\",\"source\":\"#{bold}#Relle, Cornac Fighter & Expedition Captain#{normal}#\\nNothing but hatchlings so far. Honestly, if this keeps up we won't have enough dragonhide to cover a dragon, let alone cover our losses. I've really spared no expense this time as well: Gorran is one of the finest rangers I know, and Sodelost... his prices are exorbitant, but then what else would you expect from those money-grubbing dwarven Thronesmen? I must admit I don't know much about Xann. The locals say there's no finer wyrmic in the area, and I admit she is something special in combat. Now, if only she could turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons!\",\"target\":\"#{bold}#探险队队长，科纳克人战士瑞丽#{normal}#\\n到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。老实说，照这样下去，我们得到的龙皮连一条龙都盖不住，更别说弥补损失了。这次我也确实不惜血本：高岚是我认识的最优秀的巡林客之一；至于苏达罗斯特……他的要价高得离谱，不过钢铁王座那群贪财的矮人还能是什么样？我得承认，自己并不了解希安。当地人说这一带没有比她更出色的龙战士，而她在战斗中确实不同凡响。现在只盼她能把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙！\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q030\",\"source\":\"Report for bad behavior\",\"target\":\"举报我的不良行为\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q031\",\"source\":\"Place the object where?\",\"target\":\"将物品丢弃到哪里？\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q032\",\"source\":\"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\",\"target\":\"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q033\",\"source\":\"Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.\",\"target\":\"在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q034\",\"source\":\"I will not let you down!\",\"target\":\"我一定会让你失望的！\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q035\",\"source\":\"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\",\"target\":\"竞技场生存至第20轮。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q036\",\"source\":\"Now, this is impressive!\",\"target\":\"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q037\",\"source\":\"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\",\"target\":\"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q038\",\"source\":\"Kickin' it old-school\",\"target\":\"现代风格\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q039\",\"source\":\"Killed a boss while already dead.\",\"target\":\"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q040\",\"source\":\"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\",\"target\":\"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\"}]}"}],"timestamp":1787984146324},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me go through each item.\n\nQ021: source \"which you do not understand\" — target \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" = \"even if you understand this language, you still cannot understand\". Source says \"which you do not understand\" — a language you don't understand. Target inverts: even if you understand it, you cannot understand it. That's a DIRECTION/VALUE defect. FINDING.\n\nQ022: translation seems fine. Check: \"He who shall now shatter the barriers of this world to remake it, only better!\" → \"将它重塑得更加美好\" — okay. Order of sentences matches. Fine, empty.\n\nQ023: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" — target \"凝视着他\" — \"他\" added referent; source doesn't specify. Peer out = 向外看. \"凝视着他\" adds object \"him\" not in source; peer out means look out from the slot. This is a referent/action addition. Could be FINDING: \"凝视着他\" vs \"向外窥视\". The eyes peer out — looking outward, not at \"him\". I'd report ADDITION/SUBJECT: eyes peer out (向外看), target says staring at him. Reasonable FINDING.\n\nQ024: fine.\n\nQ025: \"orbs of command\" → \"指令水晶球\" — orb = 球/宝珠; \"水晶球\" adds crystal, minor addition. Probably fine, in-game item. Hmm, orbs of command in Tales of Maj'Eyal translated as 指挥宝珠? \"水晶球\" is an addition but \"orb\" ~ ball; crystal not in source. Could be UNCERTAIN/ADDITION. But rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence and can't be judged wrong by visible evidence — crystal is not supported but orb could be crystal? \"orb\" doesn't specify material. Adding \"水晶\" (crystal) is unsupported but... rule 3 says compatible additions not a defect. Crystal vs orb — an orb isn't necessarily crystal. I'd say it's minor; leave empty? I'll leave it as no finding, maybe UNCERTAIN. I'll leave empty.\n\nQ026: fine.\n\nQ027: \"Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — \"肯定\" adds certainty; source \"I'll have everything prepared\" is future promise. \"肯定\" (definitely) addition — minor. \"which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago\" → \"那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方\" — fine. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率\" — fine. \"它\" refers to key, fine. The \"肯定\" addition — is it substantive? It changes modality slightly. Could be UNCERTAIN ADDITION. I'll maybe skip; it's minor. Actually \"I'll have everything prepared\" is a commitment; \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as \"I will definitely have everything prepared\" — fine actually, \"肯定\" = definitely will. Acceptable. Skip.\n\nQ028: \"unhallowed morass\" → \"不洁沼泽\" fine. \"inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" fine. \"find the source\" → \"找到这一切的源头\" adds \"这一切的\" — compatible. \"你效力的时候到了\" — \"you are called to serve\" — okay. Empty.\n\nQ029: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。\" — Source: only hatchlings so far (i.e., they've only found hatchlings). Target: \"never encountered hatchlings\" — INVERTED! 从未遇上 = never encountered, but source says nothing but hatchlings = only hatchlings. That's a big DIRECTION/VALUE defect. FINDING.\n\nAlso \"dragonhide to cover a dragon\" → \"龙皮连一条龙都盖不住\" fine. \"spared no expense\" fine. \"dwarven Thronesmen\" → \"钢铁王座\" fine-ish. \"wyrmic\" → \"龙战士\" fine. \"turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons\" → \"把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙\" — okay. Main finding: 从未遇上 vs nothing but hatchlings.\n\nQ030: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — adds \"我的\" (my). Source is generic \"report for bad behavior\". Hmm, likely a UI label for reporting a player's bad behavior. Adding \"我的\" changes meaning to reporting oneself. That's a SUBJECT/REFERENT defect. FINDING? Evidence supports: source has no \"my\". But could be contextually about reporting someone else... \"举报我的不良行为\" = report my bad behavior — that seems wrong; you'd report someone else's behavior. But without context, adding \"我的\" is unsupported and flips meaning. Rule 3: additions compatible with visible evidence that can't be judged wrong... \"我的\" can't be directly contradicted but it's a specific referent not in source. Actually rule 3 says new info compatible and unable to be judged wrong by visible evidence is NOT a defect. Adding \"my\" is judgeable? The source is impersonal; \"my\" makes it self-report. I'd say FINDING with SUBJECT: remove \"我的\". Hmm risky. I think it's a real defect: UI \"Report for bad behavior\" is a button to report bad behavior; \"举报我的不良行为\" is nonsense direction. I'll report as FINDING SUBJECT... Actually it could be ADDITION. I'll use ADDITION with correction \"举报不良行为\".\n\nQ031: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — \"Place\" vs \"丢弃\" (discard/drop). ACTION defect. FINDING: 丢弃 = discard, place = 放置. Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\"\n\nQ032: \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" → \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\" — adds \"在龙之贪婪成就中\" — huge ADDITION of achievement name not in source. FINDING ADDITION.\n\nQ033: fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — inverted! not let you down vs definitely disappoint. FINDING DIRECTION. Correction: \"我不会让你失望的！\"\n\nQ035: \"Got to wave 50\" → \"生存至第20轮\" — 50 vs 20, VALUE. FINDING.\n\nQ036: \"Now, this is impressive!\" → \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — adds \"这个发现\" (this discovery). Source just \"this is impressive\". Minor addition; \"this\" could refer to discovery. Compatible addition → not defect. Empty. Hmm, \"Now, this is impressive\" — could refer to anything. \"这个发现\" specific. Rule 3 allows. Empty.\n\nQ037: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" → \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心\" (ambition) loses \"power\"; \"wild\" dropped. \"权力与永恒生命的狂野梦想\". Ambition ~ dream of power? Reasonably close; \"power\" omitted but 野心 covers ambition for power? Hmm. Also \"狂野\" omitted. I'd say minor, maybe skip. Could report OMISSION of \"power\". I'll skip — 野心 reasonably implies. Empty.\n\nQ038: \"Kickin' it old-school\" → \"现代风格\" (modern style) — inverted! old-school vs modern. FINDING DIRECTION. Correction: \"复古怀旧风\" or \"老派风格\".\n\nQ039: fine. \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" fine.\n\nQ040: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" → \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"in orbit\" (轨道上) vs \"在地面上\" (on the ground) — inverted location. FINDING DIRECTION. Correction: \"使其稳定在轨道上\".\n\nAlso \"Abashed Expanse\" → \"次元浮岛\" — proper noun translated differently; without external knowledge, source is a proper name; target names it \"dimensional floating island\" — that's a rendering, can't judge without context? \"Expanse\" = 广阔区域, not 浮岛. Hmm, in ToME the Abashed Expanse is a zone. Translation \"次元浮岛\" — questionable but rule 1 says only objective issues from visible text. \"Expanse\" ≠ 浮岛 (floating island). But proper nouns are often localized creatively. Could be UNCERTAIN. The orbit/ground is clear FINDING. Maybe also UNCERTAIN for the name. I'll include one candidate for orbit/ground, maybe second UNCERTAIN for name. Actually adding it might be over-reporting. The main defect is orbit→ground. I'll include just that.\n\nQ021 correction: \"你看不懂的一种语言\" — target structure: \"which you do not understand\" modifies language. Correction: \"即使你不懂这种语言，也无法理解：...\" Hmm actually source fragment \"which you do not understand: 'Sho ch'zun...'\" — the text is in a language you don't understand. Target says even if you understand it you can't understand. Correction: \"这种语言你无法理解\" or \"你看不懂这种语言：\". I'll write: \"你无法理解这种语言：\"\n\nQ023: \"peer out\" — eyes look out through slot. \"凝视着他\" asserts gaze at \"him\". Correction: \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\". Verdict FINDING, claim ACTION or REFERENT. I'll use REFERENT? The added \"他\" plus direction. Use ACTION: peer out = 向外窥视, not staring at him. Actually two aspects: added object \"他\" and direction outward. I'll use DIRECTION or REFERENT. Pick REFERENT with correction removing 他.\n\nHmm, is it strong enough? \"peer out\" clearly means look outward from the opening. \"凝视着他\" — staring at him. Yes, direction/object contradiction. FINDING.\n\nQ025: leave empty. Actually reconsider \"orbs of command\" — in game it's 指挥宝珠. But \"水晶球\" — orb translated as 水晶球. Rule 3 protects. Empty.\n\nQ030 verdict: I'll go FINDING ADDITION? Or UNCERTAIN? The phrase \"Report for bad behavior\" — target \"举报我的不良行为\". Without context, whose behavior? Ambiguous. \"my\" is a specific addition that flips potential meaning. I think FINDING is justified: adding \"我的\" makes it self-reporting which is odd; but is it objectively wrong? Could be a button in a menu where you report the NPC's bad behavior... \"my\" would be wrong then. Given source is neutral, adding first-person possessive is an ADDITION defect. I'll report FINDING.\n\nHmm, rule 3: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\" Can \"我的\" be judged wrong by visible evidence? The source doesn't indicate whose behavior; \"my\" is compatible in the sense that the source doesn't exclude it... This rule would protect it. But the source is a generic label \"Report for bad behavior\" — the addition of a first-person referent changes the action's meaning in a way that... Honestly by the strict rules, \"my\" can't be directly contradicted. I'll mark UNCERTAIN. Hmm. Actually let me think about the source: likely a UI option when interacting with... In ToME there's \"Report for bad behavior\" maybe in p уточcases? I shouldn't rely on external. I'll go UNCERTAIN ADDITION.\n\nQ036: skip.\n\nQ037: skip. Actually reconsider \"wild dreams of power\" → \"野心\" — power omitted. \"power and eternal life\" both listed; target \"野心并获得永恒的生命\" — ambition + eternal life. Power → ambition is a narrowing but arguably compatible (ambition for power). Wild dropped. I'll skip.\n\nQ032: \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中\" — clear ADDITION FINDING. Also \"Amassed\" vs 积累 fine. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\"\n\nNow output 20 items in order Q021–Q040.\n\nFindings list:\n- Q021: FINDING (DIRECTION) — \"即使你懂得这种语言\" vs \"which you do not understand\".\n- Q022: empty.\n- Q023: FINDING (REFERENT) — 凝视着他 vs peer out.\n- Q024: empty.\n- Q025: empty.\n- Q026: empty.\n- Q027: empty (or note 肯定). Empty.\n- Q028: empty.\n- Q029: FINDING (VALUE/DIRECTION) — 从未遇上幼龙 vs Nothing but hatchlings. Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到幼龙。\"\n- Q030: UNCERTAIN (ADDITION) — 我的.\n- Q031: FINDING (ACTION) — 丢弃 vs Place.\n- Q032: FINDING (ADDITION) — 在“龙之贪婪”成就中.\n- Q033: empty.\n- Q034: FINDING (DIRECTION).\n- Q035: FINDING (VALUE).\n- Q036: empty.\n- Q037: empty.\n- Q038: FINDING (DIRECTION) — 现代风格 vs old-school.\n- Q039: empty.\n- Q040: FINDING (DIRECTION) — 地面上 vs in orbit.\n\nEvidence must be verbatim from source. Write JSON.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q021\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"DIRECTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\",\n          \"correction\": \"你无法理解这种语言\",\n          \"evidence\": \"which you do not understand\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文说的是一种你看不懂的语言（do not understand），译文反转为“即使你懂得……也无法理解”，语义方向相反。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q022\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文与原文内容、语气及语序一致，未见客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q023\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"REFERENT\",\n          \"target_span\": \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\",\n          \"correction\": \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\",\n          \"evidence\": \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文 peer out 表示眼睛从门缝向外张望，无“他”这一对象；译文添加“凝视着他”，方向与指涉对象均与原文不符。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q024\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文准确对应原文，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q025\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文完整传达原文请求与内容，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q026\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文与原文含义一致，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q027\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文信息完整，关键条件与结果均与原文相符，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q028\",\n      \"candidates\": [],\n      \"observation\": \"译文忠实传达原文指令与背景，无客观缺陷。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q029\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"FINDING\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"DIRECTION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\",\n          \"correction\": \"到目前为止只遇到了幼龙\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文 Nothing but hatchlings 表示到目前为止遇到的只有幼龙，译文“从未遇上幼龙”含义完全相反。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"Q030\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\",\n          \"claim_type\": \"ADDITION\",\n          \"target_span\": \"举报我的不良行为\",\n          \"correction\": \"举报不良行为\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Report for bad behavior\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"observation\": \"原文为泛指的“举报不良行为”，译文添加第一人称“我的”，指涉对象为原文所无，是否成立取决于未见的使用语境。\"\n    },\n    {\n